   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve given by \\( x^{2} - xy + y^{2} = 7 \\), along which \\( y \\) is a differentiable function of \\( x \\) near the point \\( (2, 3) \\). Find the value of \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} \\) at the point \\( (2, 3) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         -21,
         32
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( x^{2} - xy + y^{2} = 7 \\) implicitly with respect to \\( x \\): \\( 2 x - y + \\left(- x + 2 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\), so \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2 x - y}{x - 2 y} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "x"
               ],
               [
                  "Negate",
                  "y"
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               [
                  "Negate",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "y"
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{- 2 x + y}{- x + 2 y} \\) again with the quotient rule, treating \\( y \\) as a function of \\( x \\): \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx} - 2\\right) \\left(- x + 2 y\\right) - \\left(2 \\frac{dy}{dx} - 1\\right) \\left(- 2 x + y\\right)}{\\left(- x + 2 y\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (2, 3) \\), \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - \\frac{1}{4} \\). Substitute this value and the coordinates into the second derivative.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -21,
            32
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = - \\frac{21}{32} \\) at \\( (2, 3) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -21,
            32
         ]
      }
   ],
